<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Soni Shah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">18th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Soni Shah was a Ponwar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> who had served the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundela">Bundela</a> rulers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelkhand">Bundelkhand</a>. Around 1785 he seized Chhatarpur from the descendants of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhatrasal">Maharaja Chhatrasal</a> and founded his own state there. The British later confirmed his family in possession, and his descendants ruled Chhatarpur as a princely state until 1948.</p></div>
